{
  "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
  "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-649672e65830-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:19 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-649672e65830-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in 06-5618, Claiborne versus United States. Mr. Dwyer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-649672e65830-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What would be your test of reasonableness for appellate review?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-649672e65830-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DWYER: I think a sentence would be reasonable if a reasonable judge on the facts and circumstances of that case would find that the sentence imposed was sufficient but not greater than necessary to satisfy 3553(a) standards."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-649672e65830-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, suppose the court of appeals had done exactly what it did in this case, but it said, we're not giving any special weight whatsoever to the guidelines, we're basing this just on our own evaluation of the sentencing factors that are set out in the Sentencing Reform Act. Would there be a problem there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-649672e65830-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DWYER: I think that what guides the court of appeals on reasonableness review is to look to the particular case and determine if the reasons on the record in that case, the district court's --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-649672e65830-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Well, specifically, can you take into account, can he say I'm going to treat him as though he possessed powdered cocaine? Can he do that? Yes or no?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-649672e65830-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is the judge permitted --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-649672e65830-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: To what extent is the Congress's purpose later than the Congress that enacted the statute we're construing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-649672e65830-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government submits that the best interpretation of a reasonableness form of review would be one that conforms as closely as it can to Congress's original intent of minimizing and eliminating unwarranted sentencing disparities between similarly situated defendants."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-649672e65830-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DREEBEN: Justice Scalia, I don't think that the courts of appeals are, at least absent very unusual circumstances, to act as sentencers to specify a sentence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dwyer",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-649672e65830-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DWYER: I'm certainly going to argue that under the facts and the record before the Court, that was not a sentence that was sufficient but not greater than necessary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5618",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "649672e658307151ffc13bdb9c960d2451bf26a6ca6c195ddb67bcceef1c61c9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-649672e65830-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
